  "historyNote": "#1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss and moved by #6057-A, eff 6-30-95 (from Env-A 101.75); renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.217), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.150), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.152) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Env-A 104.39",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-A 104.39 Process weight rate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 104.39 “Process weight rate” means the smallest value obtained by computing either of the following:\n\n(a) For a continuous or long-run, steady-state source operation, the total process weight for the entire period of continuous operation or for a typical portion thereof, divided by the number of hours of such period or part thereof; or\n\n(b) For a cyclical or batch source operation, the total process weight for a period that covers a complete operation or any integral number of cycles, divided by the hours of actual process operation during such a period.\n\nSource. #1717, eff 2-19-81; ss by #2332, eff 4-29-83; ss by #2938, eff 12-27-84; ss by #5033, eff 12-27-90; ss and moved by #6057-A, eff 6-30-95 (from Env-A 101.75); renumbered by #8256 (from Env-A 101.217), (see Revision Note #1 at chapter heading); renumbered by #8304 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading); renumbered by #9839 (from Env-A 101.150), (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading); ss by #13105, eff 9-25-20 (formerly Env-A 101.152) (see Revision Note #4 at chapter heading for Env-A 100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a100.html"
